Let \mathrm{A} = \dfrac{q}{r} + \dfrac{r}{p} + \dfrac{p}{q} and \mathrm{B} = \dfrac{q}{p} + \dfrac{r}{q} + \dfrac{p}{r}.
Then,
\begin{align*}
\MoveEqLeft
\left(x+\frac{q}{r}y\right)\left(x+\frac{r}{p}y\right)\left(x+\frac{p}{q}y\right)
- \left(x+\frac{r}{q}y\right)\left(x+\frac{p}{r}y\right)\left(x+\frac{q}{p}y\right)\\
&= x^3 + \mathrm{A}x^2y + \mathrm{B}xy^2 + y^3 - \left(x^3 + \mathrm{B}x^2y + \mathrm{A}xy^2 + y^3\right)\\
&= x^3 + \mathrm{A}x^2y + \mathrm{B}xy^2 + y^3 - x^3 - \mathrm{B}x^2y - \mathrm{A}xy^2 - y^3\\
&= Ax^2y + \mathrm{B}xy^2 - \mathrm{B}x^2y - \mathrm{A}xy^2\\
&= (A-B)x^2y - (A-B)xy^2\\
&= (A-B)xy(x-y)
\end{align*}
It remains to evaluate \mathrm{A}-\mathrm{B},
\begin{align*}
\mathrm{A}-\mathrm{B} &= \frac{pq^2 + qr^2 + p^2r}{pqr} - \frac{p^2q + q^2r + pr^2}{pqr}\\
&= \frac{pq^2 + qr^2 + p^2r - p^2q - q^2r - pr^2}{pqr}\\
&= \frac{(q-r)(r-p)(p-q)}{pqr}
\end{align*}
Therefore the difference of the two products is
\frac{xy(x-y)(q-r)(r-p)(p-q)}{pqr}.

